  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Placing before or enclitic attachment",
     "texto": [
      "When there is a modal verb (**posso, vuoi, dobbiamo...**) followed by an infinitive, you have two completely equivalent options: **before the conjugated modal** (*Lo posso fare*; *Ti voglio aiutare*; *Ci deve chiamare*) or **attached to the end of the infinitive** after dropping the last vowel (*Posso farlo*; *Voglio aiutarti*; *Deve chiamarci*)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The same rule for direct and indirect pronouns",
     "texto": [
      "This freedom of position applies to both direct and indirect pronouns: **Gli voglio parlare** = **Voglio parlargli**; **La devo vedere** = **Devo vederla**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Alternating pronoun position with modals",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Pronoun before the modal",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Pronoun attached to the infinitive",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
